# Environment Variables — Names Only

Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the values.
**Never commit `.env.local` or any actual secret.**

```
# ── NextAuth ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NEXTAUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000
NEXTAUTH_SECRET=<run: openssl rand -base64 32>

# ── Firebase client (public — safe to expose) ─────────────────────────────────
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MEASUREMENT_ID=

# ── Firebase Admin (server-only — never expose) ───────────────────────────────
FIREBASE_ADMIN_PROJECT_ID=
FIREBASE_ADMIN_CLIENT_EMAIL=
FIREBASE_ADMIN_PRIVATE_KEY=<paste the key with literal \n, wrapped in double quotes>

# ── Cloudinary ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=
CLOUDINARY_API_KEY=
CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET=
CLOUDINARY_URL=cloudinary://<API_KEY>:<API_SECRET>@<CLOUD_NAME>

# ── WebSocket (print daemon) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Defaults to ws://127.0.0.1:8765 in code if unset
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PRINTER_WS_URL=ws://127.0.0.1:8765

# ── Rate limiting (optional — Upstash Redis) ─────────────────────────────────
# If unset, falls back to Firestore-based limiter
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=

# ── Cron job protection (added in R-06) ──────────────────────────────────────
# CRON_SECRET=<run: openssl rand -base64 32>

# ── Error monitoring (added in R-04) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# SENTRY_DSN=

# ── Emulator (local development only) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Set this to point Firebase Admin SDK at the local emulator instead of production
# FIRESTORE_EMULATOR_HOST=localhost:8080

# ── Danger zone ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ALLOW_DB_CLEAR=1   # Never set in production
```
